		"Students are introduced to a number of compositional techniques and are given opportunities to create original works of music and hear them performed. The course also includes listening to important 20th-century works and discussing current trends in music, the changing role of the composer in society and practical composition issues. Prerequisites: Music 112, 114, or permission of instructor."
